    <p3>
        I've been tattooing since 2018; my apprenticeship was a bit unorthodox, but, I learn so much every day, and, I plan to continue learning for as long as I can hold a tattoo machine!
        I wouldn't say I have a set style yet. Most other artists I've met just call me, "well rounded." I most enjoy tattooing in color, and my favorite styles are neotraditional and realism.
        My favorite subject matter to tattoo consists of flowers, anime, anything pop culture or "nerdy." I'm also very interested in spooky things, faces, and glitter!
        I prefer to tatoo large scale projects that take 4+ hours to complete. I just find them more fulfilling, and, I feel like I have more time to connect with the client.
        It's also very important to me that every client has a fun, relaxing experience, regardless of the level of pain! 
        I look forward to tattooing you!
    </p3>


